posts.body:
So, formula looks like this
a.level * (v[x] / 5 + 1) * (v[y] * v[y] / 100 + 1)
And I need it to be DoT damage dealt by state in JS code
v[x] is a variable for state's counter which applies to an Enemy by Actor's skills
v[y] is a variable for collected items of certain type
I tried method from
Yanfly's DoT video
but messed up with variables. Can't figure out what to put in here instead of v[x] and v[y].
For now it looks like this
<Custom Apply Effect>
// Calculate the damage to be dealt by the formula.
target._newSpace = Math.ceil(origin.level * 1 * 1);
</Custom Apply Effect>
<Custom Remove Effect>
// Remove the damage effect.
target._newSpace = undefined;
</Custom Remove Effect>
<Custom Regenerate Effect>
// Default the DoT formula.
target._newSpace = target._newSpace || Math.ceil(origin.level * 1 * 1);
// Reduce the target's HP
target.gainHp(-target._newSpace);
// Start the damage popup.
target.startDamagePopup();
// Check if the target is dead.
if (target.isDead()) {
// Make the target collapse.
target.performCollapse();
}
// Clear the target's results.
target.clearResult();
</Custom Regenerate Effect>
1's are placeholder for missing parts of original formula.

