Lets resolve it right away.
I linked
target.getStateCounter(stateID)
to a variable in a way it becomes 0 instead of NaN
And just to be sure, I did the same for the key item because there potentially might be the situation when player don't have any of these (idk if it will result NaN or 0 instead).
<Custom Apply Effect>
// Calculate the damage to be dealt by the formula.
var shards = target.getStateCounter(10) || 0;
var flowers = $gameParty.numItems($dataItems[2]) || 0;
target._newSpace = Math.ceil(origin.level * (shards / 5 + 1) * (flowers / 100 + 1));
</Custom Apply Effect>
<Custom Remove Effect>
// Remove the damage effect.
target._newSpace = undefined;
</Custom Remove Effect>
<Custom Regenerate Effect>
// Default the DoT formula.
target._newSpace = target._newSpace || Math.ceil(origin.level * (shards / 5 + 1) * (flowers / 100 + 1));
// Reduce the target's HP
target.gainHp(-target._newSpace);
// Start the damage popup.
target.startDamagePopup();
// Check if the target is dead.
// Make the target collapse.
if (target.isDead()) {
target.performCollapse();
}
// Clear the target's results.
target.clearResult();
</Custom Regenerate Effect>
Works as intended at least

